  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In March 2026 testimony, Amanda Parkhill said NCUA is using artificial intelligence for content generation, flagging anomalies in Call Report data, forecasting loan performance, identifying elevated-risk credit unions, and enhancing cybersecurity operations. She said NCUA added an AI Resources page in August 2025 that includes use cases, AI implementation, risk management, data security, and cybersecurity risks. She said NCUA is evaluating the General Services Administration’s USAi shared services and that an internal working group is assessing tools, estimated costs, use cases, and security and privacy considerations to inform its strategy. She said credit unions have expanded into AI-powered tools such as automated loan underwriting, virtual assistants, and fraud detection, and that supervisory staff must be equipped to assess both opportunities and risks.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s7",
    "s8",
    "s3",
    "s9",
    "s4",
    "s5"
   ],
